---
import SectionHeading from "../../../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../../components/Button.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Vercel Integration Documentation | KiduCode Cloud"
  description="Learn how the KiduCode Cloud Vercel integration works, including permissions, security, workflows, and how to manage your connection."
>
  <section class="section-grid py-16 lg:py-24">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Integration Guide"
      title="Vercel Integration"
      description="Connect KiduCode Cloud to your Vercel account to enable seamless deployment tracking and synchronized infrastructure management."
      as="h1"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid pb-20">
    <article class="surface-panel rounded-[28px] p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
      
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">What connecting Vercel enables</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">Connecting your Vercel account allows KiduCode Cloud Console to view your projects and deployments, providing you with real-time status updates, environment variable management, and automated deployment triggers directly from your KiduCode dashboard.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Requested permissions and why they are needed</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm leading-7">
          <li><strong>Read Projects & Deployments:</strong> To display your current deployment statuses, build logs, and active environments within the KiduCode Console.</li>
          <li><strong>Manage Environment Variables (Optional):</strong> To allow you to securely sync your local KiduCode environment variables directly to your Vercel preview or production environments.</li>
          <li><strong>Create Deployments:</strong> To allow KiduCode to automatically trigger a Vercel deployment when you approve generated code through our Cloud workflows.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Preview and production deployment workflow</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">When integrated, KiduCode can automatically link generated pull requests or code branches to Vercel preview deployments. Once a KiduCode-assisted task is merged into your main branch, KiduCode tracks the Vercel production deployment and notifies you of the build outcome within the Console.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">What information KiduCode stores</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">We store limited information to maintain the integration, specifically:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm leading-7">
          <li>Encrypted OAuth access tokens.</li>
          <li>Basic identifiers for your Vercel user/team, projects, and connected repositories.</li>
          <li>Deployment IDs, statuses, branches, and associated URLs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">For full details on data collection and retention, please review our <a href="/privacy" class="text-brand-soft hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">How credentials are encrypted</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">All Vercel OAuth access tokens are encrypted at rest using AES-256 encryption within our secure database infrastructure. Tokens are only decrypted in memory during active API requests to Vercel and are transmitted securely via TLS 1.2+.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">How to disconnect and revoke access</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">You can revoke KiduCode's access to your Vercel account at any time. To disconnect:</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm leading-7">
          <li>Go to your Vercel Dashboard and navigate to <strong>Settings > Integrations</strong>.</li>
          <li>Locate the <strong>KiduCode Cloud</strong> application.</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Manage</strong> and select <strong>Remove Integration</strong>.</li>
          <li>Once removed, KiduCode will immediately lose access, and all associated access tokens will be permanently deleted from our systems during our next automated cleanup cycle (within 24 hours).</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Troubleshooting and support</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">If you encounter any issues connecting your Vercel account or syncing deployments, please visit our <a href="/support" class="text-brand-soft hover:underline">Support page</a> or email our technical team directly at <a href="mailto:team@kiducode.com" class="text-brand-soft hover:underline">team@kiducode.com</a>.</p>
      </div>

    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
